  "body": "### Summary\n\nCheck whether the legacy-app bug \"Topic lists must not show a fake total page count\" exists in SwiftHFR (test on the lots named below) and fix it if so. Found by Bybifok (@moust4ki) in the legacy app.\n\n### Scope\n\nSwiftHFR work (from `docs/LOTS.md` \"Issues to open\" #3): LOT-022 (#50) `PageNavigation`: windowed pager = lower bound, not total (HFR-PROTOCOL §7b B1)\n\nLegacy commit: `dc93420` (see [ezzz/HFRnow#3](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/pull/3)).\n\nStatus in LOTS.md: todo.\n\n### Related lots\n\nLOT-022 (#50)\n\n### Depends on\n\n—\n\n### Credit\n\nFound by Bybifok (@moust4ki); credit the finding in the fix (label `moust4ki aka bybifok finding`). Legacy fix: ezzz/HFRnow#3 (open).\n\n### PRs\n\n- [ezzz/HFRnow#3](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/pull/3) — Bybifok's legacy-app corrections (open, not ours)\n- [ezzz/HFRnow#13](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/pull/13) — backlog of the findings in LOTS.md (merged)\n\n### Help wanted\n\n@moust4ki, you found this one: would you like to take it? The work is to check whether the bug exists in SwiftHFR (a test on the lots above) and, if it does, to fix it, with the credit to you. The code exists: LOT-022 (#50)'s `PageNavigation` and LOT-082 (#100)'s paging (only `nextPath`, never a total) are merged. Verification can start now; it may already be fixed — a test proving it is welcome.\n\nTo take it, comment `/claim <your session id>` (e.g. `/claim human/moust4ki`) and open a PR into `dev-swift` with `Closes #<this issue>` (AGENTS.md §8, CONTRIBUTING.md). If you would rather not, say so and a maintainer session will pick it up.\n",
