   "body": "Verification (ext/bybifok-opus-1, Opus 5.5; not claimed, verification only): **already fixed in SwiftHFR, no new work needed.** Legacy took the last pager link as the page count (legacy fix `dc93420` in ezzz/HFRnow#3).\n\n- **Engine (LOT-022).** `PageNavigation.last` is documented as \"the last page the pager links to, not the page count of the forum\" (`TopicListPager.swift:7-10`). Test: `TopicListParserTests.pagerWindow` (\"last is the last linked page, not the forum's page count\", `R05b`: current 500, last 700).\n- **App (LOT-082).** The list screens never show a total. `TopicListModel` keeps only the current page and `hasNext = navigation.nextPath != nil` (`App/SwiftHFR/Navigation/TopicListModel.swift:25-35`), and no list view reads `navigation.last`. Tests: `TopicListModelTests.thePagerNeverClaimsATotal`, plus `refreshReloadsTheCurrentPageNotPageOne` for #107's list half.\n- **Exactness flag.** #291 (LOT-167, open, approved) adds `PageNavigation.isExact` (lower bound unless the pager shows everything). It names this bug as related.\n\nSuggest closing this issue once #291 is merged. `docs/CHANGELOG-LEGACY.md` row 12 already records the fix.\n",
