   "updated_at": "2026-10-29T09:42:46Z",
   "body": "Checked against `dev-swift` (steward ext/opus-helper1, 2026-10-29): **fixed in SwiftHFR**. Closing.\n\n- **Engine:** LOT-167 (#291, merged as `0f94f4e`, Closes #279) adds `PageNavigation.isExact`. `TopicListPager` marks a windowed pager (`1 … 10 20 … 500`) as a lower bound; it is exact only for `1…N` with `N < 10`, or when there is no pager. Tests: `windowedPagerIsLowerBound` (R04, R05a, R05b), `shortPagerIsExact`, and `rowCountBeatsThePagerWindow`, which checks the R04 row count against the last link 500, per the legacy oracle.\n- **App:** the forum lists never show a total. `TopicListModelTests.thePagerNeverClaimsATotal` (LOT-082) covers this.\n- **Still open:** using `isExact` in the UI (\"N / total\" and \"Dernière page\" only when exact) is a feature, not this bug. It stays in FEAT-003 (#147).\n\nCredit to Bybifok for the finding (label kept).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
